1v72|a|Lax; not tense; not hard drawn; not firmly extended; as, a slack rope. ; Weak; not holding fast; as, a slack hand. ; Remiss; backward; not using due diligence or care; not earnest or eager; as, slack in duty or service. ; Not violent, rapid, or pressing; slow; moderate; easy; as, business is slack. ; Alt. of Slacken	j:33w,38,4;ult,26,2;x0g,22,6;1t1c,16,3;1wyo,14,1;1czw,6,2;1ukf,2,5~x0g,22,6;1ukf,2,5;33w,38,4;1t1c,16,3;1czw,6,2;ult,26,2;1wyo,14,1	e:qw7,18,6;22vi,17,4~qw7,18,6;22vi,17,4
